    "expect": "answer",
    "question": "Can I sit for another company after I get placed?",
    "answer": "A student who receives an offer through campus placements is considered placed and generally cannot sit for further companies [3]. \nHowever, under the dream exception, a placed student may appear for at most one more company, provided that company is in a higher category than the offer already held [3]. \nA student with a Regular offer may attempt one Standard or one Dream company, while a student with a Standard offer may attempt one Dream company [3]. \nA student who holds a Dream offer is out of the process completely [3]. \nIf the student secures the second offer, the first offer is released and the student must accept the new one, as holding two offers is not permitted [3].",
